{"success": true, "name": "arc-grid-reasoning", "file": "references/repeated-row-cycle-ordering.md", "content": "# Inferring cycle order from repeated full-width rows

When a demo turns sparse horizontal stripes into a repeated sequence of full-width rows, the output establishes what sequence was used, but not necessarily how that order or phase is derived from the test input. Record the input stripe colors and positions and the complete output row sequence separately. Check whether the demo's output cycle matches input encounter order, a rotation, reversal, or a selected subset; validate every output row and the repeat boundary.

Do not assume a cycle simply because the test contains some colors seen in the demo. If the test has a different stripe ordering and the demo does not identify the selector/order/phase rule, competing mappings remain. Since each can produce a different full output, request another example that varies the stripe arrangement before submitting. Once the mapping is established, generate rows mechanically and verify dimensions and repeated period.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792544721/attempts/cad7481303e4469588333dc46b5ca8fd/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/arc-grid-reasoning/references/repeated-row-cycle-ordering.md"}

